@startuml

title Abyss Architecture

node "Host" as Host {
  component [ACP Client\n(e.g. Zed)] as Client
  component [abyss Client Proxy] as ClientProxy
  component [Container Builder] as Builder
  component [Host Proxy\n(ACP agent side)] as HostProxy
  component [Client Plugins\n(WASM)] as ClientPlugins
}

cloud "Docker Engine" as Docker {
  node "Agent Container" as Container {
    component [abyss Agent Proxy\n(HTTP + /ws server)] as AgentProxy
    component [Container Proxy\n(ACP client side)] as ContProxy
    component [ACP Tools\n(filesystem, terminal)] as ACPTools
    component [Server Plugins\n(WASM)] as ServerPlugins
    component [Underlying Agent] as Agent
  }
}

Client --> ClientProxy : stdio (ACP JSON-RPC)
ClientProxy --> Builder : config
Builder --> Docker : Docker API\n(create, copy files,\nsetup scripts, install TLS)
ClientProxy --> HostProxy
ClientProxy --> ClientPlugins : load
HostProxy --> AgentProxy : wss (protobuf ACP,\nmutual TLS)
AgentProxy --> ContProxy
ContProxy --> ACPTools : intercept\nfs/terminal requests
ContProxy --> Agent : stdio (ACP JSON-RPC)
AgentProxy --> ServerPlugins : load
AgentProxy --> Agent : spawn (agent_command)

note right of ClientProxy
  Runs on the host as the binary
  your ACP client invokes.
  Generates an ephemeral CA and
  certificate set for mutual TLS,
  then builds and starts the
  container and proxies the
  client side of the ACP
  connection over a websocket.
endnote

note right of AgentProxy
  Runs inside the container as
  `abyss server`. Waits for a
  start file, then serves an
  HTTPS websocket endpoint and
  spawns the underlying agent,
  bridging its stdio to the
  websocket.
endnote

note right of ACPTools
  By default ACP read/write file
  and terminal requests are
  intercepted and executed
  inside the container so the
  agent can never reach the
  host. The `tools_on_host`
  config forwards them to the
  client instead.
endnote

note right of Agent
  Bring your own agent. abyss
  doesn't care what you run and
  doesn't bundle one.
endnote

note bottom of ClientPlugins
  WASM plugins see every ACP
  message on the host side and
  can transform, filter, or
  augment it.
endnote

@enduml
